{
  "title": "Wave \u2014 SaaS (6,492\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Wave\nDomain: SaaS | Scale: small | Stars: 6,492\nProblem: Wave is a Laravel-based SaaS starter kit that eliminates the need to build common SaaS features from scratch, enabling developers to quickly launch profitable SaaS applications with authentication, billing, subscriptions, and admin tools pre-built.\nTarget users: SaaS founders and entrepreneurs, Full-stack developers, Laravel developers, Indie hackers\nCore features: Authentication and User Management; Subscription Billing and Payment Processing; Role-Based Access Control and Permissions; Admin Dashboard and Management Panel; Multi-theme Support and Customization; Plugin System for Extensibility; Built-in Blog and Pages; RESTful API\nIntegrations: Payment processors (implied via billing feature), DevDojo ecosystem, Laravel Herd for installation\nTech stack: Tailwind CSS, Alpine.js, Blade templates + Laravel (PHP) + Laravel Vite\nKey libraries: Laravel, Tailwind CSS 4, Alpine.js, Axios, Tailwind Forms, Vite\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Starter kit approach: Provides opinionated, pre-configured foundation covering authentication, billing, and admin features to accelerate SaaS development\n- Modern Laravel stack: Uses Vite for asset bundling, Tailwind CSS for styling, and Alpine.js for lightweight interactivity with Laravel Blade templates\n- Extensibility-first design: Includes plugin system and theme support to allow customization without core modifications\n- Documentation-driven: Emphasizes comprehensive docs and video tutorials alongside the codebase for community adoption and developer success",
